; AmiMasterGear.config: settings for the RTG program's game screen.
; Read when the RTG program starts, from the drawer the program is in.
; One "Key = Value" a line; upper or lower case are both fine. Lines starting
; with ";" are notes. A missing line, or this whole file, means the default.
; The program icon's ToolTypes RTGSCREEN=, SCANLINES=, SCANLINESTYLE= and
; BUFFERING= (same values) win over this file, for that icon only.

; Menu: the menu opens at 1920x1080 (else 1280x720) when the graphics board
; has that mode. "Menu = Classic" gives the smaller menu (640x270, else
; 640x256) instead. Remove the ";" in front of the next line to choose it.
;Menu = Classic

; Screen: Sharp (default) opens 960x540, exactly half of 1080p, and draws the
; Master System at 2x (Game Gear 3x), so a 1080p TV shows clean square pixels.
; Bigger opens the screen mode the picture fills best and lets the graphics
; board scale it up: more of the TV filled, a little softer.
Screen = Sharp

; Scanlines: Off (default) or On, for a CRT look. They show when the picture
; is drawn at 2x or more (Sharp; Game Gear also in Bigger): the lower half of
; each game line's screen rows is the scanline.
; ScanlineStyle: how the scanline looks, the same settings as Arnold:
;   25, 50 (default), 75    Hard: the game line 25%, 50% or 75% darker
;   blendlight, blend, blendstrong
;                           Blended: the game line and the one below it
;                           mixed, then 25%, 50% or 75% darker (softer)
; (hard25, hard50 and hard75 work too.) The style is kept while Scanlines is
; Off. Arnold's single words also work in Scanlines, e.g. "Scanlines = blend"
; is On in the Blended style. The old Black is On in Hard 75%.
Scanlines = Off
ScanlineStyle = 50

; Buffering: Double (default) draws each frame out of sight and shows it in
; the display's vertical blank, so fast scrolling does not tear. Single draws
; straight to the screen (it can tear, but never misses a blank).
Buffering = Double
